    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i feel like im disappearing lately. not like physically, but just... everything that makes me \"me\" feels like it's thinning out. like i'm looking at my own life through a thick fog and i can't even remember what it felt like to actually be present in my own head. it's getting harder to recognize myself.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you're experiencing a profound sense of detachment, which is a very real and heavy feeling. This \"thinning out\" feeling is often a sign that your mind is overwhelmed, and it's understandable that you're struggling to connect with your core self. If this feeling persists, it could be beneficial to speak with a mental health professional who can offer support and guidance.",
